sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User / Client
    participant ID as interactive-designer Agent
    participant Staging as context/staging/structure.json
    participant DO as design-orchestrator Agent
    participant Runner as pipeline_runner.py
    participant Geo as geometry_engine.py (Python)
    participant Topo as topology_compiler.py (Python)
    participant Solid as cad_backend_build123d.py (B-Rep Assembly)
    participant HLR as cad_projection_hlr.py (OpenCASCADE C++)
    participant WebGL as render_presentation_webgl.py (Three.js)
    participant Composer as sheet_composer.py
    participant Export as export_cad.py (Service)
    participant Adapter as cadcraft_adapter.py
    participant CLI as vendor/cadcraft-cli (Rust Binary)
    participant Validator as cross_artifact_validator.py
    participant RedTeam as run_drawing_red_team.py
    participant Compiler as compile_package.py

    %% Phase 1: Conversational Input
    User->>ID: "I want a 14ft hexagonal gazebo with steep roof..."
    ID->>Staging: Write normalized design intent
    ID->>DO: Hand off execution

    %% Phase 2: Python Authority Execution
    DO->>Runner: run_pipeline(structure_path)
    Runner->>Geo: Stage 1: Solve 3D vertices, pitch, miter angles
    Geo-->>Runner: Return geometry._sealed = true
    Runner->>Topo: Stage 2: Validate sealed arrays & build graph
    Topo-->>Runner: Return validated topology graph

    %% Phase 3: Option C Dual-Path CAD Projection & GLB Export
    Runner->>Solid: Stage 4: build_assembly_from_structure(structure)
    Solid-->>Runner: Return TopoDS_Compound solid assembly
    Runner->>Solid: Export outputs/{project}/assembly.glb (RH_Z_UP + manifest)
    Runner->>HLR: Project blueprints (ISO, Plan, Elev, Component) via HLRBRep_Algo
    HLR-->>Composer: Return crisp occlusion-sorted vector paths
    Runner->>WebGL: Render shaded presentation (Iso, Persp, Plan, Elev) via presentation_viewer/
    WebGL-->>Composer: Return 24-bit depth-tested WebGL PNG buffers
    Composer-->>Runner: Emit 8 semantic SVG sheets to outputs/{project}/

    %% Phase 4: CAD Export & CLI Communication Boundary
    Runner->>Export: Stage 4: export_sheets(structure, output_dir)
    Export->>Adapter: export_sheet("SB01", "SB02")
    Note over Adapter,CLI: Subprocess CLI Execution Boundary (15s timeout)
    Adapter->>CLI: exec: cadcraft-cli run --cmd "..." --save "outputs/{project}/cad/..."
    CLI-->>Adapter: Return entity handles & exit code 0
    Adapter->>Export: Stamp GSD XDATA on handles (MEMBER_ID, ROLE, REVISION_ID)

    %% Phase 5: Parsed Validation Gate
    Runner->>Validator: Stage 5.5: validate_dxf_artifacts()
    Note over Validator: ezdxf readfile: Assert 0 errors, 1:1 ID parity, 3D bounds
    Validator-->>Runner: PASS ✓

    %% Phase 6: Adversarial Review & Package Compilation
    Runner->>RedTeam: Stage 5: run_drawing_red_team.py
    RedTeam-->>Runner: may_claim_success: true ✓
    Runner->>Compiler: Stage 7: compile_package.py
    Compiler-->>DO: Emits outputs/{project}/pergola_plan.pdf & CAD package
    DO-->>User: Present complete verified construction package
